Siddhamrutarasaspishta Vajrasara Mahaujasah. Like a cloud of lightning, they are the fire. 60. Meaning of the word:

Siddha-amrita-rasa-spashtaah—The demons who have been touched by the nectar of powerful yoga; Vajra-saraah—Those whose bodies are like thunderbolts;
Maha-ojasah—Extremely strong; Uttasthah—Having risen again; Megha-dalanaah—One who pierces through clouds;
Vaiduryaah—Lightning (that pierces through clouds); Iva—Like; Vahnayah—Like fire;
Vaahnayaah—Like a fire-wagon. The dead bodies of the demons became impenetrable like thunderbolts as soon as they touched this nectar. Great
Because of gaining power, they rose up like lightning that shatters the clouds.
They went. Visokya bhagnasankalpam vimanaskam vrushadhvajam. Then, Lord Vishnu thought of a means. 61. Meaning of the word

Vilokya—Seeing; Bhagna-Sankalpam—Disappointed; Vimanasakram—Extremely unhappy, distracted; Vrish-Dhwajam—To Shiva; Tada—At that time; Ayam—This; Bhagavan—God; Vishnu—Vishnu; Tatra—Near the Amrita Koop (pot of nectar); Upayam—A way (to stop);
Akalpat—Thought.
Seeing Shivji extremely sad and disappointed, Lord Vishnu thought that,
how can this calamity caused by the demon be stopped? Vatsaschaasitda Brahma swayam Vishnurayam hi Gauha. Entering the three worlds, they drank the nectar of the well. 62. Meaning of the word

Vatsah - calf; cha-bhi; aasit - became; tada - at that time; Brahma - Brahmaji; Swayam - self; Vishnu - Lord Vishnu;
Ayam - this; hi - without doubt; Gauh - cow; Pravishya - entering; Tri-puram - the three abodes; Kale - in the afternoon; Rasa-kup -
Amritam - the nectar of the well; Papau - drank. Then Brahmaji, the calf, and Lord Vishnu became cows, and in the afternoon, in the residences,
entering, they drank all the nectar from the well. Even the demons, when they see, are not enchanted. The great yogi, knowing this, is the essence of the world.
Smayanvishokah, remembering the sorrow of the bereaved, and her. 63. Meaning of the word

They—they; Asuras—a group of demons; Hi—indeed; Api—though; Pashyantah—seeing (that the calf and cow are drinking nectar);
Na—not; Nyashendh—forbidden; Vimohitah—being deluded; Tat Vijnayah—knowing this well; Maha-Yogi—great
